# Error Handling

The `onError` config callback fires whenever the active data source reports a fresh failure. It observes the data source's `queryResult`, so it works for every implementation — `FetchApiDataSource`, `ApiFunctionDataSource`, `SvelteQueryDataSource`, and any custom `IDataSource`.

Identical `Error` instances are reported only once, so a transient blip won't spam the toast queue. A different error (different identity) re-fires the callback even if the message string matches.

```typescript
const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    type: 'flakyUsers',
    columnProperties: { /* ... */ },
    dataUniquePropertyKey: 'id',
    onError: (error) => {
        // toast / sentry / console — your call
        toasts.push({ id: nextToastId++, message: error.message });
    }
};
```

| Option       | Type                       | Description                                                                                                         | Default |
|:-------------|:---------------------------|:--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:--------|
| `onError`    | `(error: Error) => void`   | Callback for data-source failures. Fires once per distinct error instance.                                          | —       |

## In-table error state

The component renders a fallback when the data source is in an error state. Replace it with the `errorState` snippet for app-specific styling:

```svelte
<DataTable {config} {dataSource}>
    {#snippet errorState({ error })}
        <div role='alert' class='alert alert-error'>
            <span>{error.message}</span>
            <button class='btn btn-sm' onclick={() => dataSource.refresh()}>Retry</button>
        </div>
    {/snippet}
</DataTable>
```

`onError` and `errorState` are independent — use both: `onError` for cross-app surfaces (toasts, telemetry), `errorState` for the contextual recovery UI inside the table.

